{"name":"update_static_dns_record","title":"Update Static DNS Record","description":"Update a static DNS record (v2 PUT static-dns/{_id}, read-merge-write).

Required: host, site, record_id and record. record_id is resolved in list_static_dns_records first; an unknown id fails listing every record and nothing is sent. record holds only the fields to change (free-form, no published schema); they are laid leaf by leaf over the listed record and the whole record is PUT. An empty update fails before any request. Returns the upstream body verbatim plus _verified (type-strict comparison of every requested leaf in a read-after) and _readAfter, or _readAfterError; a non-object write body is returned whole under response with those keys beside it. Dry-run (dry-run policy) returns a dry-run preview {status: "dry_run", dryRun, sent: false, message, preview: {method, path, params, body}}; nothing is sent.

Example call (update_static_dns_record):
    {"host": "my-console", "site": "Default", "record_id": "000000000000000000000107",
     "record": {"value": "192.0.2.21"}}

Set UNIFI_WRITE_POLICY=dry-run.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"host":{"type":"string","description":"Console name, MAC or id from list_hosts: reportedState.hostname/name (e.g. "my-console") or data[].id."},"site":{"type":"string","description":"Network site name or UUID, e.g. "Default"."},"record_id":{"type":"string","description":"Record _id from list_static_dns_records, e.g. "000000000000000000000107"."},"record":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object","description":"Fields to change, e.g. {"value": "192.0.2.21"}. Free-form object."},"confirm":{"default":false,"type":"boolean","description":"Ignored; accepted for compatibility. The call executes when made."}},"required":["host","site","record_id","record"],"type":"object"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true},"_meta":{"unifi/apiSource":"network/private.v2/write","fastmcp":{"tags":[]}}}
